[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 764,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 701,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119700,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 701,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>B-lymphoblastic leukaemia/lymphoma (B-ALL/LBL) with <em>TCF3</em>::<em>HLF</em> fusion is a neoplasm of lymphoblasts of B-cell lineage defined by the presence of rearrangement between <em>TCF3</em> at 19p13.3 and <em>HLF</em> at 17q22.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:45:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 765,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 702,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119701,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 702,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>9818/3 B-lymphoblastic leukaemia/lymphoma with <em>TCF3</em>::<em>HLF</em> fusion</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:45:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 766,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 703,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119702,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 703,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>2A70.Y Other B-lymphoblastic leukaemia/lymphoma with recurrent genetic abnormalities</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:45:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 767,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 704,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119703,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 704,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> B-lymphoblastic leukaemia/lymphoma with <em>E2A</em>::<em>HLF</em> fusion.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:45:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 768,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 705,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119704,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 705,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>B-ALL/LBL with <em>TCF3</em>::<em>HLF</em> has a distinct transcriptional profile. Rare cases of B-ALL/LBL with <em>TCF4</em>::<em>HLF</em> cluster with B-ALL/LBL with <em>TCF3</em>::<em>HLF</em> {30487223; 30643249}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:45:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 769,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 706,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119705,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 706,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>B-ALL and B-LBL represent the same disease. B-ALL always involves the bone marrow and usually also involves the peripheral blood. Extramedullary involvement is common and is by definition the primary site of involvement in B-LBL. For details, see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/63/385\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>B-lymphoblastic leukaemia/lymphoma</em> .</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:45:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 770,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 707,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119706,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 707,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Patients often present with hypercalcaemia and coagulopathy {17183364}. PTHrP plays a major role in the development of hypercalcaemia, resulting in impairment of renal function {17183364}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:45:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 771,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 708,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119707,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 708,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>B-ALL/LBL with <em>TCF3</em>::<em>HLF</em> fusion is rare across age groups (&lt;&nbsp;1% of childhood B-ALL cases) {30643249}. Most reported cases have been in children; rare cases have been described in adults {31058556; 33895809}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:45:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 772,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 709,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119708,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 709,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:45:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 773,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 710,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119709,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 710,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>The <em>TCF3</em>::<em>HLF</em> fusion couples the transactivation domains (TADs) of <em>TCF3</em> fused to the DNA-binding and dimerization domains of <em>HLF</em>. Expression of <em>TCF3</em>::<em>HLF</em> leads to transcriptional reprogramming towards an immature state. Accompanying genetic lesions, including deletion of B-cell differentiation genes (<em>PAX5</em>, <em>VPREB1</em>, or <em>BTG1</em>), deletions of <em>CDKN2A</em>/<em>B</em>, and mutations in signalling pathways driving proliferation, are frequently observed {26214592}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:45:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 780,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 717,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119710,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 717,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:45:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 774,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 711,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119711,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 711,
        "headingText": "<p>There are no unique morphological features.</p>\r\n\r\n<h5>Immunophenotype</h5>\r\n\r\n<p>CD19 expression is typically high {30765470}, but this feature is not specific.</p>\r\n&nbsp;",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:46:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 775,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 712,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119712,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 712,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:45:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 776,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 713,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119713,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 713,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Karyotype, FISH, and molecular methods are useful in establishing the diagnosis. <em>TCF3</em> break-apart FISH is not sufficient, because it cannot distinguish between <em>TCF3</em>::<em>HLF</em> and <em>TCF3</em>::<em>PBX1</em>. RT-PCR requires multiple primers to cover alternative fusion variants {8180393; 23181981; 32245383}. Next-generation sequencing of RNA, either of targeted panels or of the whole transcriptome, can identify all transcript variants.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:45:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 779,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 716,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119714,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 716,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> meets the diagnostic criteria for B-ALL/LBL (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/63/385\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>B-lymphoblastic leukaemia/lymphoma</em>); demonstration of <em>TCF3</em>::<em>HLF</em> fusion.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:45:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 777,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 714,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119715,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 714,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:45:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 778,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 715,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119716,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 715,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>B-ALL/LBL with <em>TCF3</em>::<em>HLF</em> fusion is characterized by dismal outcomes and until recently was considered incurable despite treatment intensification and allogeneic haematopoietic stem cell transplantation {26214592}. Relapse usually occurs early. In view of the high and homogeneous expression of CD19 on blasts of this leukaemia subtype, these patients may benefit from CD19-directed immunotherapy, including bispecific T-cell engager (BiTE) molecules and chimeric antigen receptor (CAR) T&nbsp;cells {30765470; 32709851}. The BCL2 inhibitor venetoclax has shown promising results in preclinical models {26214592; 28122742}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:45:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]